{
  "dom_id": "step-q135556",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "A study shows that in a particular region\n\n- there is a $62%$ chance of another rainy day after a rainy day, and\n\n- there is a $55%$ chance of another dry day after a dry day.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how the weather changes?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each day: \n\n- If it is rainy today, there is a $62%$ chance it will be rainy tomorrow. This implies that if it is rainy today, there is a $38%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow.\n\n- If it is dry today, there is a $55%$ chance that it will be dry tomorrow. This implies that if it is dry today, there is a $45%$ chance that it will be rainy tomorrow\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Rain** | **Dry** |\n| To: | **Rain** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Dry** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
